The general policy goals of the Board of Commissioners, Planning Commission and Zoning Enforcement Officer in administering this Ordinance are as follows: 23.2.1. To keep abreast of the changes in the county and to develop ideas and principals in order to make decisions based on good and up-to-date planning principals;

23.2.2. To make decisions in accordance with the comprehensive plan or any other relative plan adopted by any public agency;

23.2.3. To weigh each case on its own merit, and in doing so, attempt to be flexible rather than rigid in making a decision;

23.2.4. To attempt to centralize commercial development with adequate off-street parking than to allow congested strip development;

23.2.5. To not spot zone , thereby looking more favorable, on extensions of existing zoning districts rather than creating isolated zoning districts, unless such isolated areas are large enough to warrant the rezoning, and 23.2.6. To encourage traffic circulation within new subdivisions to be designed to connect adjoining subdivisions and to promote safety at intersections.

